  "discussion": {
    "headline": "Heavy Rain, wind to hamper thanksgiving day plans",
    "dateLine": "2:00 p.m. Tuesday, November 24, 2026",
    "excerpt": "Thanksgiving Week kicked off on a partly-to-mostly cloudy, breezy and mild note across northern MD and southeastern PA. A cold front swept through the Commonwealth on Monday and brought a few brief showers to the Lower Susquehanna Valley, but the majority of the day was dry with temperatures in the 60s. Behind the front, northerly winds of 10-20 mph have ushered a much cooler and drier air mass into the region this afternoon. …",
